extra=BeautifulSoup('''<h2>Recheck the estimate after a real change</h2><p>Repeat the comparison when you add or remove an item, change the destination, choose a different packaging instruction or receive new packed measurements. A previous screenshot belongs to its previous inputs. Keep both records when the difference is important, with a short note explaining what changed. That makes an unexpected amount easier to investigate.</p><p>For a split shipment, compare the combined payable results for every parcel. Looking at only the cheaper half hides repeated base charges and services. For consolidation, confirm that the full goods mix remains eligible and that the larger carton does not change the weight basis. The <a href="/hoobuy-consolidation-vs-split-parcels-guide-2026">consolidation and split guide</a> gives a structured comparison.</p><h2>Finish with a decision you can trace</h2><p>Before paying, save the selected route, parcel contents, packaging instructions, current measurements, displayed amount and any unresolved question. If a material field is missing, ask about that field directly. “Please confirm whether these are the final outer dimensions for this parcel” is easier to answer than “Why is shipping expensive?”</p><p>After submission, retain the parcel reference and watch for the next actual handoff. A quote, a payment and a carrier acceptance scan are separate records. Use the <a href="/hoobuy-tracking-number-domestic-international-guide-2026">tracking-number guide</a> when a shipment number becomes available. A good shipping estimate is the start of a documented decision, not proof that transport has already begun.</p>''','html.parser')
